<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boqor Osman Mahamuud</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Osman Mahamuud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boqor Osman Mahamuud was king of the Majeerteen Sultanate in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. He fought a long war with his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ali-kenadid">Yusuf Ali Kenadid</a>, who left to found the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hobyo">Hobyo</a>. In 1889 he signed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and his sultanate was conquered by Italian forces in 1927.</p></div>
